ng and test.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["src/rebar/_commands/transition.py:608-609 — `if result[\"noop\"]: sys.stdout.write(\"No transition needed\\n\")` (no-op path already prints)","src/rebar/_commands/transition.py:626-628 — `elif target_status == \"closed\": ... sys.stdout.write(f\"UNBLOCKED: {...}\\n\")` (close path already prints)","src/rebar/_commands/transition.py:612-625 — under `--output json` transition_cli emits a JSON payload with from/to/newly_unblocked/completion_signature","src/rebar/_commands/transition.py:637-653 — reopen_cli delegates to transition_cli, inheriting all of the above","Plan claims the opposite: 'transition/reopen are silent today and get NEW lines under step 1, not normalization'"],"finding":"The plan asserts transition/reopen are 'silent today' and therefore get brand-new step-1 lines rather than normalization, but transition_cli already prints to stdout on multiple paths, so the premise is refuted and the verbs are mis-categorized.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f65e621b84739e6c9","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope ('transition/reopen are silent today...'); Plan step 1 ('transition/reopen are silent today and get NEW lines under step 1, not normalization'); AC line 3 ('transition/reopen (silent today) gain step-1 lines')","norm_id":"n81c15b6b635a6789","priority":0.8,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Author implements transition confirmation as a fresh silent-verb line and drops the existing 'UNBLOCKED: <ids>' output that scripts/agents may consume","The zero-information-loss test the plan mandates for normalized verbs (create/idea/revert/claim/session-log) is NOT applied to transition, so 'newly_unblocked' data or the 'No transition needed' no-op text is silently lost"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Move transition/reopen from the 'silent today, gains NEW line' bucket into th